{
  "id": 12,
  "title": "Shopping & money",
  "goal": "Ask prices, point out 'this one' and 'that one', try things on, bargain politely and pay.",
  "intro": "Telugu has a beautifully regular set of 'pointing' words: everything near starts with **i-/ī-** (ఇది this, ఇక్కడ here, ఇప్పుడు now), everything far with **a-/ā-** (అది that, అక్కడ there, అప్పుడు then), and the question words with **e-/ē-** (ఏది which, ఎక్కడ where, ఎప్పుడు when).\n\nBargaining is normal in markets and small shops (not in malls or supermarkets). Keep it friendly: *కొంచెం తగ్గించండి* ('reduce it a little').",
